<section class="section is-small" id="media-needed">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <h2 class="title is-3 left">Media still needed</h2>
    <p class="content">Every dashed box on this page is a slot. This list repeats them in one place; delete the section once the media is in.</p>
    <ul class="checklist">
      <li><span class="num">1</span><span>Hero loop now plays the four robot rollouts back to back (cup saucer, Push-T, drawer, recycling). The Push-T segment is the low-resolution crop until the original arrives, and a GenRobot or GoPro rollout can be added once filmed.<span class="where">#top · hero.mp4</span></span></li>
      <li><span class="num">2</span><span>Method viewer, top row: a third-person source rollout for every task, and target rollouts for the GenRobot and GoPro slides. The drawer and recycling source slots show handheld or human demos as stand-ins.<span class="where">#methods · 6 source + 2 target clips, 1920×1080, 10–15 s</span></span></li>
      <li><span class="num">3</span><span>Method viewer, wrist row: four-way views (no adaptation, hide, erase, replace) for drawer and recycling, plus one GoPro wrist view. Cup saucer and Push-T are done.<span class="where">#methods · 2 × 4 clips + 1, ~10 s, wrist camera</span></span></li>
      <li><span class="num">4</span><span>Replace bank sweep: target gripper jaw sweeping on the wrist camera, then the indexed bank frames.<span class="where">#methods · 1920×1080, 8–12 s</span></span></li>
      <li><span class="num">5</span><span>Push-T third-person originals: the no-adaptation success and the erase failure now shown are crops from the video render.<span class="where">#results, #viewer, rollouts.html · 2 clips, 1920×1080, 10–15 s</span></span></li>
      <li><span class="num">6</span><span>Rollouts still missing: GenRobot cup-to-lid success and failure (third person), and GoPro-on-iPhone success and zero-shot failure.<span class="where">#results and rollouts.html · 4 clips, 1920×1080, 10–15 s</span></span></li>
      <li><span class="num">7</span><span>Hardware photos to replace stand-ins: studio 4:3 shots of each UMI finger set, the XHand with its iPhone mount beside the human wrist mount, the GoPro in the camera mount, and a photo of the deployment arm. The GenRobot image and the finger lineup clip are final.<span class="where">#design · 5 × 2400×1800 and 1 × 3000×1700</span></span></li>
